{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Scope narrowed by operator decision, then executed\n\nThe operator rejected the original 32-key disposition as too complicated for what it\nachieves, and chose the narrow path: delete the genuinely dead mechanisms, leave the live\nones alone. The description and acceptance criteria are amended to match, and the title now\nnames the actual deliverable.\n\n**Why this is not a shortcut to closing.** The reason came before the amendment, and the\nreplacement is narrower-but-real rather than a removal of verification. The ratchet check,\nthe no-new-mechanism criterion and `make verify` all survive unchanged. What was dropped is\nthe part that deletes nothing: rewording 34 markers on mechanisms that are correct and\nstaying. Editing comments does not reduce complexity — the same test that put evals out of\nscope for this program.\n\n## The sweep, measured at `origin/main` `7c3cb5e9a4f`\n\nRatchet reports `active=646 new=35 increased=0 stale=0`, exit 0. For each admitted key I\nchecked whether anything still reads the mechanism, rather than whether its sunset ticket is\nclosed:\n\n| Group | Keys | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `1e24-bfc0` Gerrit checkout-retry waits | 14 | **live** — removing them restores the false `Verified -1` they prevent |\n| `20e1-f766` job snapshot | 1 | **live** — gates nothing, but stops runner-capacity cancellations casting a false `-1` |\n| `lock::RefLockPushError` | 1 | **not a mechanism** — detector misclassification (\"an error type, not a lock\") |\n| config keys, env vars, locks, test helpers | 15 | **live** — each has readers; measured `compact.snapshot_alpha` 16, `compact.worker_log` 9, `REBAR_LLM_EMBEDDING_MODEL` 7, `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT` 16, `REBAR_LLM_SIMILAR_DIGEST_MODEL` 7 (marker lines excluded) |\n| scanner-lane, terraform tree-currency, verify-identity, user-data size | 3 | **live** |\n| `4cfc-2de2` Windows exclusive leg | 1 | **dead** |\n\n## Why the Windows step is dead, not merely redundant\n\nIts own marker states it: \"gates nothing (the job is continue-on-error) and adds no new\ncoverage — it re-runs one already-running module so its verdicts are named in the log.\"\nThree facts confirm it:\n\n- `test.yml:282` sets `continue-on-error: true`, so a failure casts no vote.\n- `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py:27` carries `pytestmark = pytest.mark.unit`,\n  so the default suite's `-m \"not integration and not external\"` selects it. The step after\n  it (`Run the default suite`) therefore already runs the module on `windows-latest`.\n- Nothing pins the step. A tree-wide grep for \"Prove the Windows exclusive leg\" returns only\n  the workflow itself. A grep for the module path across `tests/` returns the module, a\n  `pytest.mark.skipif` **reason string** at `test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py:20` (prose, not\n  an assertion), a docstring at `lock_kernel.py:54`, and two inert `dc_wiki_corpus/*.json`\n  fixtures.\n\n## What landed\n\nCommit `32021503498`, `Change-Id: I75bed3b6506d0fdefc76f3407df634231dc39979`, 1 file,\n19 deletions — the step (`:278-292`), its `mechanism-ok` marker (`:277`) and the explanatory\ncomment block (`:274-276`).\n\n**AC1 met:** admitted keys 35 → 34.\n**AC2 met:** `--check` exits 0 after the deletion. `--update-stale` is a no-op here and the\nbaseline is unchanged — the key was *admitted-new*, never baselined, so there is no shrink to\ndrain. `drain_stale` only keeps baseline keys still present, and this key was never in it.\n**AC3 met:** the change is pure deletion; nothing is added.\n**AC4 pending:** `make verify` is queued behind two other runs on this host.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793825427683337718,"uuid":"04681e4b-4ed9-43f3-9cb6-0efb8db349f1"}